submittedParameters.prompt:
Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: production world-building sprite atlas for an isometric transport management game.
Make exactly NINE separate complete miniature industry buildings, in a strict 3 by 3 evenly spaced grid on real transparent alpha. Each cell contains one independent building compound, fully inside its cell with clear transparent gutters, no adjacent parts touching. Square atlas 2048x2048 target. Each compound should occupy most of its cell, no blank top half. All the same 2:1 orthographic isometric camera, viewed from southeast, soft daylight from upper left. Ground footprints are thin rhombuses, no thick floating island sides. Architecture and equipment need readable volumes suitable for actual small game world sprites, NOT UI badges or icons.
Use first two attached images for the precise jade green/teal roof, warm ivory walls, warm gold trim, rounded elegant Taoist chibi high definition hand-painted style. Use third image for coherent world-art camera, scale, fine equipment and transportation setting. No UI frames, no text, no numbers, no plaques, no characters, no painted checkers. Genuine clean alpha.
Read left-to-right then top-to-bottom:
1 coal mine: dark coal heaps, wooden mine head winding tower and black mine opening, jade roof work shed;
2 coal power station: two brick chimneys, ivory turbine hall, black coal bay, restrained copper pipes, no smoke painted into asset;
3 sawmill: stacked cut logs and pale sawn boards, round waterwheel saw shed, teal sawmill roof;
4 managed forest logging site: small pine stand, ranger cabin and neatly stacked fresh logs, visibly forest rather than huge factory;
5 oil refinery: three cylindrical ivory process vessels, tall slender fractionation tower and gold connecting pipes, teal service building;
6 offshore oil rig: raised metal sea platform on FOUR long visible legs, drilling derrick, ivory cabins, flat small HELIPAD with a simple ring but no letters; transparent backdrop NO water;
7 general goods factory: two connected jade-roof manufacturing halls, cream brick walls, copper vent stacks, crates at loading bay;
8 printing works: distinctive folded paper rolls and finished cream sheets under canopy, compact jade-roof print workshop, gold press mechanism visible at open bay;
9 steel mill: two round red-brick blast furnaces, copper pipes, warm orange furnace opening and dark steel ingots, jade-roof casting shed.
Keep all nine distinct in silhouette and industrial equipment, not nine recolors of same house. Thin natural grey stone yards. Crisp delicate handpainting, no glossy toy-plastic appearance, no pixel art, no photorealism.

